We may consider $\mathcal A(\sigma,p,q)$ as a system of implicit atlases on $\mathcal X(\sigma,p,q)^0$ and on $\mathcal X(\sigma,p,q)^1$ separately.  Now consider the following maps (where the complexes on the left are defined analogously to those on the right as in \S\ref{SSaugmentedsec}):
\begin{align} C^\bullet_{\mathrm{vir}}(\partial\mathcal X^0,\mathcal A)^+&\oplus C^\bullet_{S^1,\mathrm{vir}}(\partial\mathcal X^1,\mathcal A)^+&&\to C^\bullet_{\mathrm{vir}}(\partial\mathcal X;\mathcal A)^+\\ C^\bullet_{\mathrm{vir}}(\mathcal X^0\operatorname{rel}\partial,\mathcal A)^+&\oplus C^\bullet_{S^1,\mathrm{vir}}(\mathcal X^1\operatorname{rel}\partial,\mathcal A)^+&&\to C^\bullet_{\mathrm{vir}}(\mathcal X\operatorname{rel}\partial;\mathcal A)^+
